2097, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 899, "last_played": 1676042935, "avatar": "e315c2a6786f19483dd678dd5cc325dc20a7945e"}, "language": "english", "review": "Amazing game. Honestly, it is very tough to say a game is perfect, but this gets very close. \n\nTL;DR @ bottom.\n\nPros:\n+Pretty up to date textures\n+Nice amount of weapons that you can choose from\n+Smooth controls (I would recommend a gamepad if you have one, although M&Key is OK.)\n+Pretty great soundtrack\n++Amazing voice work\n+++One of your Ultramarines looks like Anthony Hopkins\n+Decently long game\n+Plenty of multiplayer content\n\nCons:\n-Due to THQ going bankrupt, there will be no sequel to this *planned* trilogy. (Ends on insanely annoying cliffhanger) \n-The online playerbase is a bunch of elitist neck-beards that hate new players\n-Even on the hardest difficulty, the game was still pretty simple\n\n\nThis game is all around pretty solid for 29.99. For all the DLC as well, it is 59.99, and completley NOT worth it. Pick this up on a sale, and get the full collection if you really enjoy multiplayer. This game definitley requires that you join a group to have fun with multiplayer. \n\nIf you've wanted to get into Warhammer 40,000, I'd say this is one of the CHEAPEST ways to do so and enjoy it. This is just scraping the surface of the Lore 40k has to offer. I honestly recommend this to anyone looking for a good 3PS. \n\ntl;dr:\n\nGreat 3rd Person Shooter, feels a bit like GoW with less clunkly movement. Game is stupid difficult without a built in 'cover' function, but still very fun. Pick it up on a sale, and only get DLC if you like multiplayer games.", "timestamp_created": 1421037614, "timestamp_updated": 1421037614, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.528382003307342529", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}]}